  "description": "Codex: Adeptus Custodes (11e) AQUILA COMMANDER (WP-C3): at the start of the battle round, if your WARLORD has the ability, gain 1CP. Fixture cus11e_c3_custodes_active: round 2, P1 Custodes take the first turn, WARLORD = the Shield-Captain (Aquila Commander), 6 CP each. (1) Loading the save starts battle round 2: P1 gains 1CP (Command phase) + 1CP (Aquila Commander) = 8, P2 (WARLORD Warboss) only 7; the scoreboard reads CP:8 and the game log names Aquila Commander. (2) Setup privilege: jump to the END of the Orks' turn (Scoring phase, active player 2). (3) A real click on the phase button ends the Orks' turn: battle round 3 begins with the Custodes Command phase and Aquila Commander fires again — P1 10 CP (+1 phase, +1 Aquila), P2 8 CP (+1 phase), the bonus CP recorded against the 1-per-round cap.",
  "fixture": "cus11e_c3_custodes_active",
  "edition": 11,
  "rng_seed": 42,
  "disable_ai": true,
  "martial_katah": true,
